Backport upstream mujs 1.3.11 hardening to the bundled thirdparty/mujs
copy (which is verbatim upstream 1.3.10).

The bundled thirdparty/mujs in mupdf 1.28.6 is byte-identical to the
standalone mujs 1.3.10 tarball from mujs.com (jsarray.c md5
15160a65518590fe2256f1c396b14e7e matches 1.3.11 as well, since
jsarray.c did not change in 1.3.11). The 1.3.10 -> 1.3.11 delta is
6 files (jsrun.c, jscompile.c, jsi.h, jsregexp.c, regexp.c, main.c);
this backports the 5 security-relevant files and intentionally leaves
out the main.c shell usage-message hunk (commit 01a75ff4, "-R/-M flags
in usage"), which only fixes help text of the standalone mujs shell
and is not compiled into libmupdf (the library builds thirdparty/mujs
via one.c, which does not include main.c).

Hunks, all verified against the mujs.com 1.3.11 tarball
(sha256 456a395769daf110a30f9bf6f793044261e261481d5dca33b63cdc8714774ca4,
md5 4f1bf51428bdea3175adbf63e55b693e; 1.3.10 sha256
6e36c15dbb84ff859320297c900852f241b131a7b6ddaea669ac9a65bd75571c):

- thirdparty/mujs/jsrun.c jsR_isindex: range-check-first. Check
  v->u.number against 0..INT_MAX before casting to int, avoiding
  undefined behavior on out-of-range doubles when testing whether a
  value is a valid array index.
  Upstream: codeberg.org/ccxvii/mujs commit 8a32c397
  ("Fix undefined behavior casting out-of-range int to double").

- thirdparty/mujs/jsrun.c jsR_unflattenarray: fix error recovery.
  On exception, delete any array entries already migrated to the
  property tree instead of NULLing obj->properties (which leaked and
  left a NULL dereference later). Mark the loop index volatile.
  Upstream: codeberg.org/ccxvii/mujs commit e744aaa1
  ("Fix error in recovering from errors when unflattening simple
  array").

- thirdparty/mujs/jscompile.c stm->jumps handling (Bug 709757):
  unlink each jump entry as it is freed so an exception from labelto()
  cannot double-free the head of the list.
  Upstream: codeberg.org/ccxvii/mujs commit aab59f2c
  ("Bug 709757: Don't double free when labeljumps gets an exception").

- thirdparty/mujs/jsi.h + jsregexp.c + regexp.c: regexp integer
  hardening. Widen js_RegExp flags/last from unsigned short to int,
  compare re->last as size_t against strlen(), and use size_t for the
  regexp program-size computation (count()/n) so inputs longer than
  64k cannot overflow into a negative "program too large" check.
  Upstream: codeberg.org/ccxvii/mujs commits 4bff9635
  ("Fix size_t to int implicit casts in regexp") and d0e82695
  ("Fix integer overflow when regexp operates on strings longer
  than 64k").

After this backport the shipped library code (everything pulled in via
thirdparty/mujs/one.c) is byte-equivalent to upstream mujs 1.3.11 in
all security-relevant paths; only the standalone-shell usage text
differs.

